d 'XTIE2': module to provide Fixed-effects panel interactions, conditional effects, and Johnson–Neyman regions
d
d     xtie2 fits xtreg, fe with all pairwise interactions among the
d explanatory variables. By default the first two explanatory	
d variables are the focal pair. pair() selects any two explanatory
d variables and internally places them first; the fitted model	 
d is unchanged by this ordering. All explanatory variables are
d treated as continuous. For the focal conditional effects, the   
d remaining explanatory variables enter through their interactions
d with the focal variables and are held at their   
d estimation-sample means. Declare the panel with xtset first. This
d command does not estimate Hansen-type panel thresholds.    For a
d model with x1, x2 and additional variables zk, the effect of x1
d at x2=v, holding each zk at its estimation-sample mean,    is b1
d + b12*v + sum_k b1k*mean(zk). The effect of x2 is analogous.
d Standard errors use the full covariance matrix of these   
d coefficients. No causal interpretation is implied by the command. d
d KW: panel data
d KW: interactions
d KW: marginal effects
d
d Requires: Stata version 17
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260929
d
d Author:  Zehra Yalnız,   Kocaeli University, Türkiye
d Support: email zehrayalnizz41@@gmail.com
d
d Author:  Figen Büyükakın,   Kocaeli University, Türkiye
d Support: email NA
d
f xtie2.ado
f xtie2.sthlp
